1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,920
You do everything for everyone.

2
00:00:03,281 --> 00:00:04,421
Does anyone even care?

3
00:00:06,341 --> 00:00:07,842
Martha asked Jesus that.

4
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:10,082
She had opened her home to Him.

5
00:00:11,102 --> 00:00:13,603
While she served, her sister Mary sat at His

6
00:00:13,643 --> 00:00:14,403
feet and listened.

7
00:00:15,663 --> 00:00:18,083
Lord, dost thou not care that my sister hath

8
00:00:18,144 --> 00:00:19,404
left me to serve alone?

9
00:00:19,964 --> 00:00:21,764
bid her therefore that she help me.

10
00:00:22,444 --> 00:00:23,004
His answer?

11
00:00:24,445 --> 00:00:24,905
Her name.

12
00:00:26,325 --> 00:00:26,725
Twice.

13
00:00:28,085 --> 00:00:31,446
Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled

14
00:00:31,506 --> 00:00:34,767
about many things: But one thing is needful:

15
00:00:35,467 --> 00:00:38,187
and Mary hath chosen that good part, which

16
00:00:38,227 --> 00:00:39,828
shall not be taken away from her.

17
00:00:39,848 --> 00:00:42,208
"Careful" means full of worry.

18
00:00:43,328 --> 00:00:46,249
Mary had chosen the one thing needed: to listen

19
00:00:46,289 --> 00:00:46,629
to Him.

20
00:00:47,689 --> 00:00:49,190
And He would not send her away.

21
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:52,530
So, did He care?

22
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,991
Later, the Bible says this about Martha, Mary

23
00:00:57,231 --> 00:01:00,552
and their brother: "Now Jesus loved Martha,

24
00:01:00,912 --> 00:01:04,993
and her sister, and Lazarus." He did not call

25
00:01:05,053 --> 00:01:06,093
Martha's work wrong.

26
00:01:06,793 --> 00:01:09,073
Under all her work, He saw her worry.

27
00:01:09,813 --> 00:01:10,734
And He loved her.
